    '|a||Ask why anyone sells a car they bought a week ago. Maybe they changed their mind. Or maybe they found out it''s a lemon.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:d2efmi'
    '|b||Lemon is American slang for a dud. A good one, economists call a peach.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:rbc0wo'
    '|a||Only the owner knows which one it is. To a buyer, peaches and lemons look the same on the lot.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:7gdnbl'
    '|a||So the buyer can only pay for an average car, with the chance of a lemon priced in.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:18of3he'
    '|b||Which is a bad deal for anyone selling a peach. Why let a good car go at a lemon-tinted price?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1jij8sp'
    '|a||So peaches stay home, and the cars for sale get worse. That''s where the trouble starts.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:p7auz3'
    '|a||If peaches stay home, how far does the damage go? Line up ten used cars, from a near-wreck to almost new.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7840
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Each owner knows what theirs is worth: from almost nothing up to ten thousand dollars. Illustrative numbers.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:lyjjxg'
    '|a||Buyers can''t tell the cars apart, but a car is worth more to a buyer who needs one. Akerlof''s own example: half as much again.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:13x8k0c'
    '|b||With every car on sale, the average is worth five thousand. So buyers offer one and a half times that: seven and a half.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:vsxuhx'
    '|a||At seven and a half thousand, the owners of the best cars say no thanks. They keep them.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:8hwk6p'
    '|b||Now the cars left for sale are worse on average, and the buyers know it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:hz5oqh'
    '|b||So what will buyers offer next? Click the line where you think the next offer lies.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:7kgrd5'
    '|a||About five thousand six hundred. The cars left average three seven fifty, and half again is fifty-six hundred.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||And now the next-best owners leave. Round after round, the offer falls and another car drops out.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:a9ubf7'
    '|b||Akerlof''s words: the bad driving out the not-so-bad, driving out the medium, until no market exists at all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1uv3bxa'
    '|a||Yet in every round some buyer would gladly pay more than some owner wants. Trades that help both sides never happen.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:iza3ub'
    '|a||Your turn: step through the rounds yourself, then raise how much more buyers would pay. Find where the market stops unravelling.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:b9fwq1'
    '|a||Want to see why two is the line? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3880
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Buyers offer one and a half times the average car on sale.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3680
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||If cars worth up to P are on sale, the average is worth half of P. So the next offer is three quarters of P.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1bihr1n'
    '|a||Each round shrinks the offer by a quarter, all the way down. Only if buyers pay double or more does it hold.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:96izvg'
    '|a||Strip away the cars and the unravelling is a loop. Quality is hidden, so everyone gets one price.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||At that price the best walk away, so the average falls, the price falls, and round again.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:pgzzpk'
    '|a||Akerlof''s point was that the loop fits any market where one side knows more than the other. And it isn''t always the seller.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:qkvzlm'
    '|a||Try it. Who knows more about the quality: the one selling, or the one buying? Sort each case.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:zq9fhi'
    '|b||Insurance was his first example: there the buyer knows his own health better than the insurer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Hiring too. An employer who can''t see a worker''s skill may judge by a group label instead, and the skilled in that group lose out.':
